      "title": "Polymorphism",
      "lectureOrder": 60,
      "videoOrder": 59,
      "sourceHash": "6b76f6525928668d0f30ebc592a6aad728f6f56636baf71e40ca96b4b0f694d6",
      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 3.81,
          "en": "(light calming music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.81,
          "end": 6,
          "en": "-: In this video, let's talk about polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 8.01,
          "en": "Remember we have talked about method overriding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.01,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "and then we say there's something more?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 11.7,
          "en": "This is where we are talking about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 15.45,
          "en": "So we have a concept of polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.45,
          "end": 18.09,
          "en": "Now this is a very important concept in terms of OOPs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.09,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "and most of the languages which implements OOPs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "has this concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 23.58,
          "en": "Now, what is polymorphism?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 23.58,
          "end": 26.37,
          "en": "Now basically as a concept, it has two words.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.37,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "One is poly, second is morphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 33.95,
          "en": "Now poly simply means many, and morphism means behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.35,
          "end": 36.63,
          "en": "Now what it means is there's something which behaves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.63,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "differently in different situatio based on situation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "Let's say as a human,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "you behave differently at different locations, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "Example, for at home, I behave differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "At my office, I behave differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 52.14,
          "en": "When I'm with my friends, I behave differently, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.14,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "So that situation changes me in the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "because the name also changes right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "At home, I'm a son, husband, a father,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 64.233,
          "en": "at office, I'm a colleague, I'm a boss, I'm an employee,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 65.67,
          "end": 66.81,
          "en": "with my friends, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.81,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "They use different words, but then let's not mention that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 71.03999999999999,
          "en": "So the important thing is your behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.03999999999999,
          "end": 72.81,
          "en": "your name changes at every place, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.81,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "Your behavior changes based on that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.19,
          "en": "In the same way in the world of object oriented,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.19,
          "end": 79.89,
          "en": "we have a concept of many behavior, polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.89,
          "end": 82.83,
          "en": "So the same object or the same reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.83,
          "end": 84.21000000000001,
          "en": "will have different behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 84.21000000000001,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "based on how you create the instance of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "Now, to implement this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 90.84,
          "en": "there are multiple ways in different languages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 90.84,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "But before we go into the implementation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 94.41,
          "en": "let's talk about its type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 94.41,
          "end": 96.93,
          "en": "So there are two types of polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 96.93,
          "end": 100.68,
          "en": "One is called a compile time polymorphism,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 100.68,
          "end": 103.32,
          "en": "and second is called a runtime polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 103.32,
          "end": 104.555,
          "en": "Of course, they have different names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 104.555,
          "end": 107.88,
          "en": "Compile time is also called early binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 107.88,
          "end": 109.97999999999999,
          "en": "runtime polymorphism also called late binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 113.16,
          "en": "But we have these two words, compile time and run time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 113.16,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "Now what do you mean by compile time?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 116.67,
          "en": "See if you can define your behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 116.67,
          "end": 119.7,
          "en": "So the behavior is defined at compile time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 119.7,
          "end": 121.44,
          "en": "that is compile time polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 121.44,
          "end": 123.72,
          "en": "If the behavior will be defined at run time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "that is called a run time polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 127.89,
          "en": "So when you compile the file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 127.89,
          "end": 131.1,
          "en": "and when you know what thing will get executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 131.1,
          "end": 133.41,
          "en": "at the compile time itself, it is compile time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 135.21,
          "en": "Now, which method will be executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 135.21,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "will be decided at run time, that's run time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 140.19,
          "en": "Now we have done two examples here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 140.19,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "which is overloading and overriding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 145.11,
          "en": "So if you talk about overloading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 145.11,
          "end": 146.61,
          "en": "it's a part of compile time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 146.61,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "because at the compile time itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 150.06,
          "en": "example, let's say if you have two methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 150.06,
          "end": 152.1,
          "en": "you have, let's say two methods,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 157.1,
          "en": "which is add, which takes two parameters, int and int.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "And then we have one more method here, which is add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "And when you say int, int, int,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "which takes three parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 168.42000000000002,
          "en": "Now both this have the same name, but different parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 168.42000000000002,
          "end": 170.1,
          "en": "That is method overloading.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 170.1,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "Now, which method to execute?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "Will you execute the first or second method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 175.41,
          "en": "will be decided at compile time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 175.41,
          "end": 176.91,
          "en": "Now, let's say you have two classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 176.91,
          "end": 179.94,
          "en": "class A and class B to add two different classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 179.94,
          "end": 182.01,
          "en": "And class B extends class A.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 182.01,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "We have talked about this in method overriding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 187.02,
          "en": "And let's say you have a method which is add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 188.82,
          "en": "which takes two parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 188.82,
          "end": 191.28,
          "en": "And also here we also have the add method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 191.28,
          "end": 193.38,
          "en": "which takes two parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 193.38,
          "end": 196.95,
          "en": "Now, out of these two, which one will get executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 196.95,
          "end": 198.09,
          "en": "it will be decided at run time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 198.09,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "So that is called run time polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 201.93,
          "en": "In fact, there's one more concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 201.93,
          "end": 204.09,
          "en": "which we're going to discuss in the implementation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 204.09,
          "end": 206.52,
          "en": "when we talk about dynamic method dispatch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 206.52,
          "end": 208.92000000000002,
          "en": "at that point, this thing will get more clear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 208.92000000000002,
          "end": 210.84,
          "en": "But just to generalize, what is polymorphism?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 210.84,
          "end": 212.97,
          "en": "Polymorphism means many behavior.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 212.97,
          "end": 215.04,
          "en": "So your behavior of your reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 215.04,
          "end": 218.7,
          "en": "or your execution will change based on some situation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 222,
          "en": "If it is compile time, which is your method overloading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 222,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "where you decide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "based on the parameters at compile time itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 228.78,
          "en": "in runtime, you're not sure which method will be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 228.78,
          "end": 230.82,
          "en": "because both the methods have the same name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 230.82,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "same parameters, something which will decide that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 234.78,
          "en": "we'll discuss in the next video.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 234.78,
          "end": 236.46,
          "en": "But that is method overriding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 236.46,
          "end": 238.207,
          "en": "which is run time polymorphism.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
